# Commit Message Offer

After completing code changes (unless the user already asked you to commit), end with a ready-to-paste commit message.

## Format

1. One line only (no body unless they ask).
2. Prefer `type: short summary` (`fix`, `feat`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`).
3. Imperative, lowercase after the type, ~50 characters max (hard cap 72).
4. No em/en dashes. No period at the end unless needed for clarity.
5. Fence as `text` with only the message line (no `git commit` wrapper).

## Examples

```text
fix: utf-8 encoding in GithubConnectCard
```

```text
chore: timeout hung alembic in ci deploy
```

## When not to

- Read-only questions with no file changes.
- User already asked to commit (create the commit instead).
- Nothing left to commit.
